.TH REDHAT-AI-CONFIGURATOR-OPENCODE 1 "November 2026" "redhat-ai-configurator-opencode 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
redhat-ai-configurator-opencode \- install and configure OpenCode for Red Hat AI MaaS (rhai-maas) and EnMaaS
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B redhat-ai-configurator-opencode
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B redhat-ai-configurator-opencode
configures the
.BR opencode
AI coding agent with the user's own Red Hat AI MaaS and EnMaaS API keys.
When OpenCode is not installed, the tool downloads the current Linux release
and installs it in \fB~/.local/bin\fR (override with \fB--install-dir\fR).
Run it without arguments for the interactive terminal installer.
.PP
The tool validates each key against the service before writing anything,
stores the key through \fBopencode auth import\fR, merges its settings into the
existing \fBopencode.json\fR, and backs up every file it replaces. It never
creates API keys: you create them in the browser.
.PP
Service endpoints are configured rather than embedded. Set them with
\fB--rhai-maas-base-url\fR and \fB--enmaas-base-url\fR, in
\fI/etc/redhat-ai-configurator-opencode/endpoints.conf\fR, or through the
environment variables listed below. Flags win over the environment, which wins
over the file. A fresh install uses placeholder example.com values and warns
until they are replaced.
.PP
Red Hat AI MaaS needs the corporate VPN to be
.BR off ;
EnMaaS needs it
.BR on .
The installer shows which is required at each step.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-non-interactive
Run without prompts. Implied by \fB--yes\fR, \fB--dry-run\fR and a non-TTY.
.TP
.BR \-y ", " \-\-yes
Accept defaults without prompting.
.TP
.BI \-\-provider " ID"
Providers to configure, comma separated: \fBrhai-maas\fR, \fBenmaas\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-rhai-maas-base-url " URL"
Base URL for \fBrhai-maas\fR, including \fB/v1\fR. Overrides the environment
and \fIendpoints.conf\fR. Rejected unless it starts with \fBhttp://\fR or
\fBhttps://\fR and ends with \fB/v1\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-enmaas-base-url " URL"
Base URL for \fBenmaas\fR, the host root without \fB/v1\fR. Overrides the
environment and \fIendpoints.conf\fR. Rejected if it includes \fB/v1\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-key-file " PATH"
Read \fINAME=value\fR lines from PATH, or \fB-\fR for stdin. The file must be
mode 0600 and owned by the invoking user. Recognised names are
\fBRHAI_MAAS_API_KEY\fR and \fBENMAAS_API_KEY\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-keep-existing
Reuse a key that is already stored instead of requiring it again.
.TP
.BI \-\-model " PROVIDER=MODEL"
Set the default model, for example \fBenmaas=rits/zai-org/glm-5-3\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-agent " AGENT"
Primary agent OpenCode starts with: \fBbuild\fR (default) or \fBplan\fR.
.TP
.BI \-\-install-dir " DIR"
Download OpenCode into DIR when it is missing. Default: \fB~/.local/bin\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no-install
Never download OpenCode; fail when it is not installed.
.TP
.B \-\-no-validate
Do not call the services to check keys. Useful for offline image builds.
.TP
.B \-\-require-validation
Fail when a key could not be validated, for example on the wrong VPN. Also
refuses to write a configuration whose selected provider still has a placeholder
endpoint (exit 2).
.TP
.B \-\-no-verify
Do not run \fBopencode models\fR afterwards.
.TP
.B \-\-rollback-on-failure
Restore the previous configuration if verification fails. Accounts already
imported into OpenCode's credential store are kept.
.TP
.B \-\-dry-run
Print what would change and exit without writing.
.TP
.BI \-\-format " text|json"
Output format. JSON is intended for automation.
.TP
.BI \-\-config-dir " DIR"
OpenCode configuration directory. Default: \fB~/.config/opencode\fR, or
\fB$XDG_CONFIG_HOME/opencode\fR when that variable is set.
.TP
.B \-\-doctor
Check the current configuration without changing it.
.TP
.B \-\-list-models
Print the models the service offers, then exit.
.TP
.B \-\-allow-root
Permit running as root. Containers and image builds only.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B RHAI_MAAS_API_KEY
Red Hat AI MaaS API key.
.TP
.B ENMAAS_API_KEY
EnMaaS API key. It also serves the \fBenmaas-oai\fR (Gemini) provider.
.PP
An environment key wins over the same name in \fB--key-file\fR; an unset or
blank variable counts as absent. The interactive installer does not read these
variables and asks for the key instead.
.TP
.B RHAI_MAAS_BASE_URL
OpenAI-compatible base URL, including \fB/v1\fR.
.TP
.B ENMAAS_BASE_URL
Anthropic-compatible root, without \fB/v1\fR (the installer appends \fB/v1\fR).
.PP
\fB--rhai-maas-base-url\fR and \fB--enmaas-base-url\fR override these values.
.TP
.BR RHAI_MAAS_KEY_PAGE ", " RHAI_MAAS_HELP_URL
Page for creating a key, and the help link shown in the UI.
.TP
.BR ENMAAS_KEY_PAGE ", " ENMAAS_HELP_URL
Page for creating a key, and the help link shown in the UI.
.TP
.BR ENMAAS_ELIGIBILITY_URL ", " ENMAAS_SLACK
Optional access-request page and help channel.
.TP
.B OPENCODE_CONFIG_DIR
Relocates OpenCode's configuration directory; useful in tests.
.TP
.B OPENCODE_INSTALL_BASE
Mirror for the OpenCode release tarballs. The platform file name is appended.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, or a successful dry run.
.TP
.B 1
Unexpected error.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error: bad flag or base URL, placeholder endpoints with
\fB--require-validation\fR, no provider, or no TTY without
\fB--non-interactive\fR.
.TP
.B 3
OpenCode is missing, older than 2.0, or could not be downloaded.
.TP
.B 4
A key is missing, unreadable, or was rejected.
.TP
.B 5
A service is unreachable (network or VPN).
.TP
.B 6
A configuration file, credential import, or download could not be written.
.TP
.B 7
The configuration was written but \fBopencode models\fR did not list the
configured models.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/redhat-ai-configurator-opencode/endpoints.conf
Service endpoints. Flags and environment variables take precedence.
.TP
.I ~/.config/opencode/opencode.json
Providers, models, default model and default agent. Merged, backed up before
writing.
.TP
.I ~/.local/bin/opencode
Default install location for a downloaded OpenCode CLI.
.PP
Keys are stored in OpenCode's own credential store (its SQLite database) through
\fBopencode auth import\fR. The tool never edits that database directly.
.SH EXAMPLES
Configure both providers from environment variables:
.PP
.nf
export RHAI_MAAS_API_KEY=...
export ENMAAS_API_KEY=...
redhat-ai-configurator-opencode --non-interactive --provider rhai-maas,enmaas
.fi
.PP
Configure both providers without editing
\fIendpoints.conf\fR or exporting base URLs (keys still come from the
environment or \fB--key-file\fR):
.PP
.nf
redhat-ai-configurator-opencode --non-interactive --provider rhai-maas,enmaas \\
  --rhai-maas-base-url https://maas.example.com/v1 \\
  --enmaas-base-url https://enmaas.example.com
.fi
.PP
Read keys from stdin and emit machine-readable output:
.PP
.nf
printf 'RHAI_MAAS_API_KEY=%s\\n' "$KEY" |
  redhat-ai-configurator-opencode --non-interactive --provider rhai-maas \\
  --key-file - --format json
.fi
.SH NOTES
Run the tool as the user who will use OpenCode, not as root. Keys are created by
the user in the browser; the tool only validates and stores them.
.SH SEE ALSO
OpenCode documentation: https://opencode.ai/v2/docs/
